# $project_id

A [pluginlake](https://github.com/plugin-healthcare/pluginlake) project package.

This project plugs into a pluginlake node through a single `ProjectManifest`
(see `src/$package_name/manifest.py`) and owns one DuckLake catalog
(`$catalog`) and asset-URN namespace (`$namespace`).

## Develop

```bash
uv sync
uv run pluginlake verify   # conformance check
uv run pytest
```

## What it contributes

- **Config:** `$config_prefix`-prefixed settings (`src/$package_name/config.py`).
- **Dagster code location:** `$package_name.definitions` (ingestion assets).
- **API routers:** mounted uniformly by the core gateway.
- **Connectors:** framework-agnostic data connectors (`src/$package_name/connectors.py`).

Core interprets the manifest and mounts these within the project's namespace and
the authn/authz scope; the project never mints bare endpoints.
